ns / fuel_pressure_governor_derivative_gains through working copies on the stack (each gain scaled by its lookup table while cam_timing_alt_mode_enable_cal is 0); the base command uses fuel_metering_uncompensated_duty_cycle_proportional_gains and fuel_metering_current_compensation_derivative_gains; the trim uses fuel_metering_current_compensation_proportional_gains and fuel_metering_current_compensation_integral_gains. The copy of the derivative record's negative window is one 4-byte store at offset 16 that runs 2 bytes past the 18-byte record - so Ghidra prints a raw stack or register name for its destination. Was cm848_calculateEngineTimingOffset Quirk (disassembly): only governor mode 1 (OPEN_LOOP_START) sets r29 - the start temperature chosen by engine_sync_state_b; modes 2 / 4 and the fixed-command modes 8 / 16 / 32 / 64 jump past it, so the integrator-preset lookup at 0x48ba8 (taken while engine_rpm_measured is 0) reads the caller's r29 (the unaff_r29 argument). Likely harmless: it only runs with the engine stopped and mode 1 recomputes the preset before a start.
